14286,"explanation":"Hippopotamus: 5 m (upper adult length). Person: 1.75 m (reference height). Ratio: 2.86×.\nHippos measure about 3.3–5 m long. This board uses the upper end.","sources":["https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/hippo","Reference chosen for comparison: a 1.75 m person."],"tag":"Nature / Reference"},{"id":"how-much-ish-v4-89","version":4,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the ingenuity helicopter to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Ingenuity helicopter","dimension":"rotor tip-to-tip span","shape":"sourced:ingenuity"},"reference":{"name":"US dollar note","dimension":"approximate note length","shape":"sourced:dollar-note","measure":"0.156 m · approximate note length"},"bounds":[0.01,100],"answer":7.69230769,"explanation":"Ingenuity helicopter: 1.2 m (rotor tip-to-tip span). US dollar note: 0.156 m (approximate note length). Ratio: 7.69×.\nThe Mars helicopter’s counter-rotating rotors span about 1.2 m from tip to tip.","sources":["https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","https://www.federalreserve.gov/aboutthefed/chapter-1-balance-sheet.htm"],"tag":"Space / Everyday"},{"id":"how-much-ish-v4-90","version":4,"kind":"scale","prompt":"Resize the webb sunshield to match its real size.","target":{"name":"Webb sunshield","dimension":"deployed sunshield length","shape":"sourced:webb"},"reference":{"name":"Steinway Model D","dimension":"piano length, plan view","shape":"sourced:concert-grand","measure":"2.74 m · piano length, plan view"},"bounds":[0.01,100],"answer":7.73722628,"explanation":"Webb sunshield: 21.2 m (deployed sunshield length). Steinway Model D: 2.74 m (piano length, plan view). Ratio: 7.74×.\nThe unfolded sunshield is approximately 21.2 by 14.2 m. This profile compares its long axis, not the mirror diameter.","sources":["https://science.nasa.gov/mission/webb/science-overview/science-explainers/telescope-overview/","https://www.steinway.com/dam/jcr%3A9d156c27-487d-478c-8d2d-4dda7d47475b/918_Steinway